    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 3.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="496–497" ed="#liebermann"/>En Denelahe VIII lib. le forfeit, les XX sol. pur la teste, les VII lib. al rei.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="496–497" ed="#liebermann"/>E<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.4"/> en Denelae le forfait<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.5"/> VIII livres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.6"/>, les XX solz pur la teste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.2"/>, e les VII livres al rei.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="496–497" ed="#liebermann"/>At uero in Denelahe in tali casu forisfactum est VIII librarum, quarum VII regis erunt, octaua autem pro capite calumpnia[n]ti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.b"/> dabitur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="3.3" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="254" ed="#robertson"/>En Denelahe, VIII lib. le forfeit, les XX sol. pur la teste, les VII lib. al rei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="496–497" ed="#liebermann"/>3, 3. Im Dänen-Rechtsgebiet 8 £<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_3-3.lnote.de.1"/> die Verwirkung: die 20 Schill. statt des Kopfs [des Angeklagten an den Kläger] (und <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) die 7 £ dem König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">3, 3. In the Danish legal district 8 £ the forfeiture: the 20 shill. in place of the head [of the accused, to the plaintiff] (and <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) the 7 £ to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="255" ed="#robertson"/>In the Danelaw a fine of £8 [shall be paid]—20 shillings in lieu of the head [of the accused man] and £7 to the King.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 254–255 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 496–497, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">496</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">test <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">test Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">496</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cent <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> E en <hi rend="italic">Hs. Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cent instead of E en MS Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">496</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-feit <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-feit Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">496</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">liueres <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">liueres Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">497</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">calumpniati <hi rend="italic">S, zwar auch richtig, aber, weil selbstverständlich, kaum durch L eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">calumpniati S, correct, it is true, but, being self-evident, hardly inserted by L</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_3-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">287</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. 24. Ein Hundert (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6) Silbers</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. 24. A hundred (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6) of silver</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
